  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the radius of curvature of the common internal film surface of the double bubble formed by two bubbles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/0051525_di.JPG\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 164px;\" /><br /><br />Excess of pressure as compared to the atmosphere inside&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.03</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Excess of pressure inside&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.04</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />In the double bubble, the pressure difference between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> on either side of the common surface is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.03</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.04</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10233;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.03</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.04</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10233;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.03</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.04</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.01</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.12</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
